  AC -9 is not nearly good enough in the lower levels.  AC's better than
-40 are possible, and I wouldn't think of going into Hell with worse
than -25.

  If you're in Wizard mode, try wishing for a stethoscope.  You can apply
it to monsters and see what their attributes are, especially how many
hit points they have left.  It's especially useful on the wiz . . .

  Another way to beat him is to use Stormbringer -- it drains a level
each time it hits, so he can't just teleport away and come back as
strong as before.  But killing him is not necessarily the best thing
to do . . . 

  Boots of speed are another necessity in the lower levels.  So is a
cloak of magic protection, and the right rings and amulets will make
things a lot easier.

  The problem with playing in discovery mode is that when you're immortal,
you don't worry about dying, so it's easy to just wade through without
thinking about what you're doing.  That leads to lots of unnecessary
deaths.

